.TH SHB-CONFIG 1 "October 2026" "SecretHarbor 0.4.0-prod" "SecretHarbor Manual"
.SH NAME
shb-config \- Inspect and manage effective policy configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBshb config [show|check|edit|diff|source] [options]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspects what SecretHarbor intends to enforce. `shb config` and `shb config show` are strictly read-only and never print secret values. `shb config edit` is a human-only operation protected against agent execution.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
\fBcheck\fR
Checks the project policy file for YAML syntax errors, rule contradictions, and invalid presets.
.TP
\fBdiff\fR
Visualizes the customizations in the current project compared to SecretHarbor's base standard security preset.
.TP
\fBedit\fR
Opens the project policy in $EDITOR. Protected by a strict security boundary: sandboxed agents are denied execution to prevent policy tampering.
.TP
\fBget\fR
Reads and displays the current configuration value for a specified key (e.g. protection, guard, secrets.mode, network.mode).
.TP
\fBset\fR
Updates and validates a configuration setting in project policy file. Sandboxed agents are denied execution.
.TP
\fBshow\fR
Displays the effective policy with all defaults, presets, and overrides resolved. Never reveals secret credentials.
.TP
\fBsource\fR
Displays rule provenance and lineage, showing whether a rule originated from a preset, built-in detection, or project file override.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
$ \fBshb config\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb config --json\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb config source\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb config check\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb config edit\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb config diff\fR
.SH SEE ALSO
shb(1)
